{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\WINDOWS\\\\System32\\\\WindowsPowerShell\\\\v1.0\\\\powershell.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content -Encoding UTF8 C:/Users/emper/.codex/model-routing-notes.md; herdr agent list; herdr pane read w4:pB --source recent-unwrapped --lines 18'","aggregated_output":"# Routing evidence and local operation\r\n\r\nVerified 2026-09-10. These notes support AGENTS.md; read only when relevant. Recheck live official information before relying on prices or product behavior in a new model-selection task.\r\n\r\n## Astra low versus Sol\r\n\r\nTibo (@thsottiaux), 2026-09-06 19:55 UTC, said Astra low performs better than Sol high and recommended Astra low/medium for people satisfied with Sol high. The post does not publish comparative token counts, wall-clock measurements, or a universal cost result. It does not compare Astra low against Sol low.\r\n\r\n- Original: https://x.com/thsottiaux/status/2096688770523467947\r\n- Text was verified through the public mirror because X returned HTTP 403: https://x.noodl3.net/thsottiaux/status/2096688770523467947\r\n\r\nOpenAI's Astra release reports reduced output-token use on ExploitGym, about 47% less task time in OSWorld 2.0 latency simulations (roughly 40 versus 75 minutes), and Terminal-Bench 4.0 scores of 57.9% versus Sol's 37.3% at approximately 9% lower estimated API cost per task. These are different evaluations and configurations, not controlled Astra-low versus Sol-high measurements. The overall score table reports maximum scores at any effort.\r\n\r\n- https://openai.com/index/gpt-6-astra/\r\n\r\nAPI Standard short-context rates per million tokens were Astra $10 input / $50 output and Sol $4 input / $20 output. Astra's comparable token rates are 2.5 times Sol's. Lower reasoning effort may reduce generated tokens and retries but does not itself lower the per-token tariff. For equal token composition/tier, approximately 60% fewer billable tokens is the break-even point; actual input, output, cached tokens, and retries must be accounted for separately. Sol promotional pricing was stated to last at least through 2026-11-21. Subscription allowance accounting is not equivalent to API dollars or raw token counts.\r\n\r\n- https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/pricing\r\n- https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-5.6-sol\r\n- https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/pricing\r\n\r\nRouting judgment: use Luna/Terra for bounded routine work; try Astra low directly for difficult coding likely to need Sol high or expensive retries; retain Sol low/medium where it meets acceptance at a lower measured or reasonably expected total cost. Prefer observational telemetry from useful tasks over duplicate benchmark runs.\r\n\r\n## Configuration and Windows launch\r\n\r\nGlobal default in `config.toml`: `gpt-5.6-terra`, reasoning `low`. Final review preset: `review-max.config.toml`, selected by `codex --profile review-max`. Existing sessions retain their selected model/effort. These instructions govern behavior; they are not a continuously running scheduler.\r\n\r\n- Global instruction loading: https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/agent-configuration/agents-md\r\n- Original config backup: `backups/herdr-cost-policy-20260910/config.toml.093856757.bak`.\r\n\r\nLocal Herdr smoke check: created sibling pane wB:p2 with `--no-focus`, confirmed a Codex Terra-low agent, and completed policy drafting and web research through `herdr agent prompt`/`wait`/`read`.\r\n\r\nObserved launch issue: `herdr agent start` used Windows `Start-Process -FilePath codex`; PATH resolved to `codex.ps1`, causing an invalid-Win32-application error. If this same failure recurs, inspect the named agent and pane first. When the created pane is back at its available PowerShell prompt, use `herdr pane run <observed-pane-id> 'codex --model <model-id> -c model_reasoning_effort=<effort> --no-alt-screen'`, retaining the authorized sandbox settings. Then verify detected agent, mode